Phoenix’s JavaScript client provides programmatic access to datasets used in AI evaluation workflows. Its release adds typed helpers for dataset labels within the existing datasets scope, allowing callers to manage reusable global labels rather than handling only individual dataset assignments.

Callers can first manage the shared label resources and list them using cursor pagination, which retrieves successive pages through a continuation marker. They can then assign or replace labels on a dataset selected by name or GlobalID. The compact release note documents those operations, without describing automatic labeling, label-based access controls or measured workflow improvements.

