## LangWatch bounds trace-field retrieval to protect workers

Source: LangWatch · GitHub — https://github.com/langwatch/langwatch/releases/tag/langwatch%40v3.22.0
Published: 2026-11-02
Channel: github

LangWatch is an AI observability and evaluation platform whose release notes include fixes to reading trace data. One entry bounds recall of offloaded fields so that large traces cannot kill the worker handling them. Offloaded-field recall means retrieving trace content that has been stored separately.

A second entry says a span’s own attributes no longer break its read through a request-parameter name. A span is the record of one operation within a trace. These notes identify two read-path corrections, but do not state the retrieval limit, affected payload sizes or measured memory savings. They are selected trace-reliability changes from a broader platform release.

Why it matters: For LangWatch operators handling large traces: check representative trace reads after upgrading and verify that expected fields remain available.

